PRICE ELASTICITY – TELECOM TRANSACTION DATASET
BUSINESS SCENARIOS AND STRATEGIC VALUE
==============================================================

DATASET STRUCTURE
-----------------
This is a transaction-level telecom recharge dataset.

Price  = transaction_amount
Demand = Refill frequency per subscriber
Time   = transaction_timestamp

Each row represents one recharge transaction made by a subscriber.

Elasticity measures how refill frequency changes when price changes.



BUSINESS SCENARIOS BASED ON PRICE ELASTICITY

1) HIGHLY PRICE ELASTIC CUSTOMERS
Definition:
When price increases, refill frequency drops significantly.

Business Actions:
- Offer smaller denomination packs.
- Provide targeted discounts.
- Avoid aggressive price increases.

Business Benefit:
- Protect transaction volume.
- Prevent revenue loss.


2) PRICE INELASTIC CUSTOMERS
Definition:
Price changes have little impact on refill frequency.

Business Actions:
- Introduce premium bundles.
- Slightly increase prices.
- Upsell higher-value packs.

Business Benefit:
- Increase ARPU.
- Improve overall revenue.


3) SEGMENT-BASED ELASTICITY
Elasticity varies across segmentation_id or service_class.

Business Actions:
- Apply segment-based pricing.
- Personalize promotions.
- Target offers per customer group.

Business Benefit:
- Higher profitability through smart pricing.


4) TIME-BASED ELASTICITY
Customer sensitivity changes over time.

Business Actions:
- Run promotions during high-sensitivity periods.
- Adjust pricing during peak seasons.

Business Benefit:
- Revenue optimization through timing.


5) SERVICE CLASS ELASTICITY
Elasticity varies by service class.

Business Actions:
- Maintain affordability for basic users.
- Upsell premium users.

Business Benefit:
- Balanced revenue strategy.


6) AGENT-LEVEL IMPACT
Elasticity differs across voucher agents.

Business Actions:
- Incentivize high-performing agents.
- Monitor agent-level refill trends.
Business Benefit:
- Channel performance optimization.


7) REVENUE OPTIMIZATION
Revenue = Price × Quantity

If Elasticity > 1 (Elastic):
Price increase → Revenue decreases

If Elasticity < 1 (Inelastic):
Price increase → Revenue increases

Business Use:
- Simulate pricing changes before implementation.
- Reduce financial risk.


8) CUSTOMER BEHAVIOR PROFILING
Identify:
- Frequent small refill users
- Occasional high-value users
- Premium customers

Business Actions:
- Loyalty programs
- Personalized bundles
- Retention strategies

Business Benefit:
- Improved customer lifetime value.



